  "text_input": "Patient was apparently asymptomatic 2 days back, then developed fever which was insidious in onset and gradually progressive, associated with chills and rigors. Patient had taken antipyretics, following which fever subsided temporarily and recurred after stopping medication. No diurnal variation noted. Fever was associated with generalized myalgia since 2 days. Patient also complains of cough since 1 day, which was sudden in onset and gradually progressive. No aggravating or relieving factors. Cough is associated with expectoration which is scanty in amount, mucoid in consistency and whitish yellow in colour. No complaints of chest pain or breathlessness. No complaints of orthopnoea or PND. No complaints of loose stools or vomiting. No complaints of any bleeding manifestations or rashes. No complaints of burning micturition, decreased urine output, or increased frequency of micturition.",
